    "text": {
     "en": "In a series circuit the components are joined one after another. If one bulb fuses, all go off.\nIn a parallel circuit the components are on separate branches. If one fails, the others keep glowing.\nHouses use parallel wiring so that each appliance can work on its own."
    }
